---
// The applicant's status page.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT OPENS IT
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The reference AND the private key issued when the application was started.
// Not reference plus contact email: references are sequence-allocated, so the
// next one along is always guessable, and a school's contact address is usually
// printed on its own website — both halves of that pair are public and what
// they would unlock is the school's own submission.
//
// Changing the ref in the address bar therefore reaches nothing. The key is
// bound to one application, and applicantStatus() in src/db/applications.ts
// compares it in constant time against the row the reference selected. A wrong
// key and an unknown reference are the same answer here, deliberately: telling
// them apart would make this page an oracle for which references are real.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// WHAT IT SHOWS
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The stage the case has reached, and every entry the federation marked visible
// — no routing, no lead score, no internal notes, no owner. The filter is a SQL
// predicate in applicantStatus(), not a pass over the rows here, so an internal
// note never reaches this process at all.
//
// The timeline is rendered by CaseTimeline, which also renders the
// administrator's view of the same case at /admin/applications/{id}. One
// renderer, two row sets, and the row sets differ only by the stored
// visible_to_applicant flag — so the two halves of a case cannot describe it
// differently.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// AND NOW: THE REST OF THE CHAIN, AND THE QUOTATION ITEMISED
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// A timeline says what has happened. It does not say what the request IS — and
// a school that has been quoted wants the quotation, not a line reading
// "quotation issued". So this page now also reads, for this one application and
// no other:
//
//   · the quotation raised against the training request it produced, at its
//     current version, ITEMISED — the fee engine records the rule, the
//     quantity, the unit amount, the factor and the running total for every
//     line, and a total with no working shown is a number to be argued with;
//   · the agreement, if one has been signed, and the programme, if delivery has
//     started.
//
// WHICH VERSIONS ARE THE APPLICANT'S TO SEE, AND WHICH ARE NOT.
// A quote version at `draft` or `awaiting_approval` is INTERNAL. It is a figure
// the federation is still deciding about — in the second case, a figure a rule
// deliberately held for a second person to look at — and showing it here would
// hand the applicant a number nobody has agreed to and would quietly defeat the
// approval that fee module exists to enforce. The predicate is in the WHERE
// clause, and it is the same set of statuses the client portal honours:
// issued, accepted, rejected, expired, superseded.
//
// Where a NEWER internal version exists, this page says a revision is being
// prepared and shows no figure for it. Saying nothing would leave the school
// reading a superseded amount as though it were current.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// NO DATE IS PROMISED, AND NO AMOUNT IS INVENTED
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// MMAKF has published no service standard for institutional applications, so
// slaDueAt is null on every row and the "respond by" line does not render. The
// page says what has happened. It never says when the next thing will, and it
// never marks anything late — there is no published deadline for anything here
// to be late against.
//
// MMAKF has also published no fee framework. computeFee() can therefore price
// nothing, every application ends at "a quotation will be prepared", and this
// page shows NO AMOUNT AT ALL for one — not a placeholder, not an estimate and
// above all not a zero, because zero reads as FREE and is the most expensive
// misunderstanding available here. A quote version carrying
// requiresManualQuote has no number, and what is printed in its place is the
// fact that no published rule covered the request.
//
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// THE SECOND READ OF THE APPLICATION ROW
// ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// applicantStatus() does not return the application's id or its training
// request, and it should not: it is the applicant's view and neither is a fact
// about their case that they need. But the quotation hangs off the request, so
// this page reads those two columns itself — AFTER applicantStatus() has
// already verified the key in constant time and thrown if it did not match.
//
// That ordering is the whole safety argument and it is not incidental. The
// second read runs only on the authenticated path, so it introduces no oracle:
// a wrong key never reaches it. And it selects TWO COLUMNS BY NAME rather than
// the row, so the owner, the lead score, the routing decision and the access
// token itself never enter this process at all — the same rule applicantStatus()
// follows, applied to the query this page had to write for itself.

import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Status from '@/components/Status.astro';
import CaseTimeline from '@/components/CaseTimeline.astro';
import { and, asc, eq, inArray } from 'drizzle-orm';
import { isConfigured, db } from '@/db';
import * as s from '@/db/schema';
import * as ops from '@/db/operations.schema';
import { applicantStatus, TOTAL_STEPS } from '@/db/applications';
import { formatINR, PPM } from '@/db/fees';
import { href as surfaceHref, type Surface } from '@/lib/surface';

export const prerender = false;

const surface: Surface = (Astro.locals as any)?.surface ?? 'public';
const h = (p: string) => surfaceHref(surface, p);

const ref = String(Astro.params.ref ?? '');
const token = Astro.url.searchParams.get('k') ?? '';
const justSent = Astro.url.searchParams.get('sent') === '1';

// The address of this page CONTAINS the key. Two consequences, both handled
// here rather than trusted to a default:
//
//   · no-store, because a shared or cached copy of this page is a copy of one
//     school's contact details, requirements AND — now — the amount it has been
//     quoted;
//   · no-referrer, because every link a reader follows off this page would
//     otherwise carry the key to wherever they went, in the Referer header.
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'no-store, private');

// KEPT OUT OF SEARCH BY A HEADER, NOT BY A <meta> IN THE TEMPLATE.
//
// This page used to say so with `<meta name="robots" … slot="head" />`. Base.astro
// defines exactly ONE slot — an unnamed `<slot />` inside its main landmark —
// and Astro silently DISCARDS content addressed to a named slot a layout does
// not define.
// So the directive never reached the document, and the page said "never indexed"
// in a comment while shipping no robots directive at all.
//
// Base.astro's own noindex does not cover it either: that fires on
// `isPrivatePath()`, and /learn/applications is not one of PRIVATE_PREFIXES —
// correctly, because /learn is a public section. The route is kept out of the
// sitemap, which is what hid the gap: tests/seo-live.test.ts only inspects URLs
// the sitemap advertises.
//
// What this page renders is ONE institution's own submission — its contact
// rows, its requirements, its case timeline and its quoted amounts — reachable
// with the key in the address. An applicant who pastes that link into a forum
// or a shared document must not thereby publish their application.
//
// A response header cannot be dropped by a layout change, which is why the
// three sibling private surfaces (/pay/[token], /application, /learn/portal)
// all set it this way.
Astro.response.headers.set('X-Robots-Tag', 'noindex, nofollow');
Astro.response.headers.set('Referrer-Policy', 'no-referrer');

let view: any = null;
let failure: string | null = null;

// The commercial half of the case, all of it null until a row says otherwise.
let quoteRef: string | null = null;
let quoted: any = null;              // the current version the applicant may see
let quoteLines: any[] = [];
let revisionInProgress = false;      // a newer version exists and is internal
let firstQuotationInProgress = false; // a quotation exists and none is issued yet
let agreement: any = null;           // contracts row
let programme: any = null;           // training_programs row
let commercialProblem: string | null = null;

if (!isConfigured()) {
  failure = 'The federation’s database is not reachable from this deployment, so this application cannot be looked up.';
} else {
  try {
    view = await applicantStatus(db(), ref, token);
  } catch (err) {
    // Deliberately the same message for a wrong key and a reference that does
    // not exist. See the note at the top.
    failure = 'No application matches that link. Check the address, including the part after ?k=.';
  }
}

/**
 * The statuses of a quote version the applicant may be shown.
 *
 * `draft` and `awaiting_approval` are absent and their absence is the point:
 * a number the federation has not issued is not a number the applicant has
 * been given, and a version a rule held for approval is one the federation has
 * deliberately not agreed to yet.
 */
const VISIBLE_QUOTE_STATUSES = ['issued', 'accepted', 'rejected', 'expired', 'superseded'] as const;
const INTERNAL_QUOTE_STATUSES = ['draft', 'awaiting_approval'] as const;

// A draft is not an application. It has been started and not sent, and the only
// useful thing this page can offer is the way back into the form — so nothing
// commercial is read for one either.
const isDraft = !!view && view.status === 'draft';

if (view && !isDraft) {
  try {
    // TWO COLUMNS, BY NAME. See the note at the top of this file.
    const [row] = await db()
      .select({
        id: ops.institutionApplications.id,
        requestId: ops.institutionApplications.requestId,
      })
      .from(ops.institutionApplications)
      .where(eq(ops.institutionApplications.ref, view.ref))
      .limit(1);

    if (row?.requestId != null) {
      // Every version of the one quotation raised against this request, oldest
      // first. Quotes are never edited — they are re-versioned — so "the
      // quotation" is the newest version the applicant is entitled to see, and
      // the older ones keep their own figures for the record.
      const versions = await db()
        .select({
          quoteRef: s.quotes.ref,
          quoteId: s.quotes.id,
          id: s.quoteVersions.id,
          version: s.quoteVersions.version,
          status: s.quoteVersions.status,
          subtotalMinor: s.quoteVersions.subtotalMinor,
          discountMinor: s.quoteVersions.discountMinor,
          concessionMinor: s.quoteVersions.concessionMinor,
          taxMinor: s.quoteVersions.taxMinor,
          totalMinor: s.quoteVersions.totalMinor,
          currency: s.quoteVersions.currency,
          requiresManualQuote: s.quoteVersions.requiresManualQuote,
          validUntil: s.quoteVersions.validUntil,
          issuedAt: s.quoteVersions.issuedAt,
        })
        .from(s.quoteVersions)
        .innerJoin(s.quotes, eq(s.quoteVersions.quoteId, s.quotes.id))
        .where(eq(s.quotes.requestId, row.requestId))
        .orderBy(asc(s.quotes.id), asc(s.quoteVersions.version));

      if (versions.length) {
        const visible = versions.filter((v: any) =>
          (VISIBLE_QUOTE_STATUSES as readonly string[]).includes(String(v.status)));
        quoted = visible.length ? visible[visible.length - 1] : null;

        // ── THE REFERENCE COMES OFF THE VERSION BEING SHOWN ────────────────
        //
        // It used to come off `versions[0]`, and that was only ever right
        // because a request was assumed to have one quotation. `quotes` has no
        // unique index on request_id — migration 0048 adds one, and until it is
        // APPLIED to a deployment the rows this reads may still contain two
        // quotations for one request, each numbering its versions from 1. This
        // page would then have printed one quotation's reference beside another
        // quotation's amount: a school reading a reference the federation would
        // look up and find a different figure against.
        //
        // A reference and a figure are only ever safe to print together when
        // they come off the same row. So they do. And every comparison below is
        // confined to the quotation being shown, because "version 2" of one
        // quotation says nothing about version 1 of another.
        quoteRef = quoted ? quoted.quoteRef : versions[versions.length - 1].quoteRef;

        const sameQuote = (v: any) =>
          quoted == null || Number(v.quoteId) === Number(quoted.quoteId);

        const internal = versions.filter((v: any) =>
          (INTERNAL_QUOTE_STATUSES as readonly string[]).includes(String(v.status)));

        // A newer internal version means the federation is working on a
        // revision. The applicant is told THAT and given no figure for it.
        revisionInProgress = quoted != null
          && internal.filter(sameQuote).some((v: any) => Number(v.version) > Number(quoted.version));

        // A quotation exists and nothing has ever been issued from it. Also
        // said outright: a school that has been told "we are quoting you" and
        // sees nothing here would reasonably think the page is broken.
        firstQuotationInProgress = quoted == null && internal.length > 0;

        if (quoted && !quoted.requiresManualQuote) {
          // The arithmetic, in the order it was performed. sortOrder is the
          // sequence the fee engine wrote, so the running total climbs down the
          // page exactly as it climbed through the computation.
          quoteLines = await db()
            .select({
              sortOrder: s.quoteLines.sortOrder,
              kind: s.quoteLines.kind,
              label: s.quoteLines.label,
              quantity: s.quoteLines.quantity,
              unitAmountMinor: s.quoteLines.unitAmountMinor,
              factorPpm: s.quoteLines.factorPpm,
              amountMinor: s.quoteLines.amountMinor,
              runningTotalMinor: s.quoteLines.runningTotalMinor,
              sourceKind: s.quoteLines.sourceKind,
            })
            .from(s.quoteLines)
            .where(eq(s.quoteLines.quoteVersionId, quoted.id))
            .orderBy(asc(s.quoteLines.sortOrder));
          // `ruleCode` and `because` are DELIBERATELY not selected. They are the
          // federation's own rule identifiers and the raw condition keys that
          // matched — "participants 80 is within 50–100; mode is on_campus" —
          // written for an administrator reading /admin/quotes. What makes the
          // figure legible to a school is the label, the count, the unit price
          // and the running total, and those are here.
        }
      }
    }

    if (row?.id != null) {
      const [c] = await db()
        .select({
          ref: ops.contracts.ref,
          status: ops.contracts.status,
          startsOn: ops.contracts.startsOn,
          endsOn: ops.contracts.endsOn,
          signedAt: ops.contracts.signedAt,
          programId: ops.contracts.programId,
        })
        .from(ops.contracts)
        .where(and(
          eq(ops.contracts.applicationId, row.id),
          // A draft agreement is internal for the same reason a draft quotation
          // is: it is a document the federation is still writing.
          inArray(ops.contracts.status, ['issued', 'signed', 'active', 'completed', 'terminated', 'expired'])
        ))
        .orderBy(asc(ops.contracts.id))
        .limit(1);
      agreement = c ?? null;

      if (c?.programId != null) {
        const [p] = await db()
          .select({
            code: s.trainingPrograms.code,
            title: s.trainingPrograms.title,
            status: s.trainingPrograms.status,
            startsOn: s.trainingPrograms.startsOn,
            endsOn: s.trainingPrograms.endsOn,
            sessionsPlanned: s.trainingPrograms.sessionsPlanned,
          })
          .from(s.trainingPrograms)
          .where(eq(s.trainingPrograms.id, c.programId))
          .limit(1);
        programme = p ?? null;
      }
    }
  } catch {
    // A commercial read that failed must not take the status page down with it.
    // The stage and the timeline are the reason the school opened this address.
    commercialProblem =
      'The quotation and agreement records for this application could not be read just now. ' +
      'Nothing has changed and nothing has been lost — this was a read that failed. ' +
      'The progress below is unaffected.';
  }
}

const resumeStep = Math.min(Math.max(Number(view?.stepReached) || 1, 1), TOTAL_STEPS);
const resumeHref = view
  ? `${h('/learn/apply')}?ref=${encodeURIComponent(view.ref)}&k=${encodeURIComponent(token)}&step=${resumeStep}`
  : h('/learn/apply');

function when(v: unknown): string {
  if (!v) return '';
  const d = new Date(v as string);
  if (Number.isNaN(d.getTime())) return '';
  return d.toLocaleDateString('en-IN', { day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric' });
}

/**
 * Money, or nothing at all.
 *
 * null rather than a zero when there is no figure — see the note at the top.
 */
const money = (minor: unknown, currency: unknown = 'INR'): string | null => {
  if (minor == null || typeof minor !== 'number' || !Number.isFinite(minor)) return null;
  const cur = String(currency || 'INR');
  return cur === 'INR' ? formatINR(minor) : `${cur} ${(minor / 100).toFixed(2)}`;
};

/** One line of the quotation, in the words the fee engine's own record supports. */
function lineWorking(l: any): string {
  if (l.kind === 'multiplier' || l.kind === 'tax') {
    return `× ${(Number(l.factorPpm) / PPM).toFixed(4)}`;
  }
  if (l.quantity != null) {
    return `${l.quantity} × ${formatINR(Number(l.unitAmountMinor ?? 0))}`;
  }
  return '';
}

// ─── The chain, as the applicant sees it ────────────────────────────────────
//
// EVERY STAGE IS EVIDENCED BY A ROW. Nothing below infers one stage from
// another: "accepted" is not assumed because an agreement exists, and
// "in delivery" is not assumed because an agreement was signed. Each is a
// predicate over a stored value, and where there is no row the stage is simply
// not reached.
//
// It is drawn as the route the federation's process takes and said, in words,
// not to be a promise that this application travels all of it. That is the
// honest form: CaseTimeline deliberately renders no forward rail because a
// stage drawn ahead of a case reads as a commitment it will be reached, which
// is false for every application that is declined or withdrawn. So the ladder
// below is labelled as the route, a stage that has not happened carries no date
// and no estimate, and when the case has ENDED the remaining stages are not
// drawn at all.

const ENDED_STATUSES = ['declined', 'withdrawn', 'expired'];
const hasEnded = !!view && ENDED_STATUSES.includes(String(view.status));

// The stored status values that mean a person at MMAKF has the case open. Read
// from the column, not inferred from the passage of time.
const IN_HAND = [
  'acknowledged', 'under_review', 'information_requested',
  'program_design', 'quoted', 'proposed', 'approved', 'contracted',
];

interface AppStage {
  key: string;
  label: string;
  reached: boolean;
  /** What is true, in the applicant's words. Never a forecast. */
  detail: string;
}

const stages: AppStage[] = !view || isDraft ? [] : [
  {
    key: 'sent',
    label: 'Sent',
    reached: !!view.submittedAt,
    detail: view.submittedAt
      ? `Received by MMAKF on ${when(view.submittedAt)}.`
      : 'Not recorded as sent.',
  },
  {
    key: 'in-hand',
    label: 'With the federation',
    reached: IN_HAND.includes(String(view.status)),
    detail: IN_HAND.includes(String(view.status))
      ? 'Someone at MMAKF has this application open.'
      : 'Nobody at MMAKF has picked this up yet.',
  },
  {
    key: 'quoted',
    label: 'Quotation issued',
    reached: !!quoted,
    detail: quoted
      ? (quoted.requiresManualQuote
          ? `Quotation ${quoteRef} was raised and carries no amount — see below.`
          : `Quotation ${quoteRef}, version ${quoted.version}, is set out below.`)
      : firstQuotationInProgress
        ? 'A quotation is being prepared. Nothing has been issued to you yet.'
        : 'No quotation has been issued.',
  },
  {
    key: 'acceptance',
    label: 'Waiting on you',
    reached: !!quoted && String(quoted.status) === 'issued',
    detail: quoted && String(quoted.status) === 'issued'
      ? 'The quotation stands and MMAKF is waiting for your answer.'
      : 'Nothing is waiting on you.',
  },
  {
    key: 'accepted',
    label: 'Accepted',
    reached: !!quoted && String(quoted.status) === 'accepted',
    detail: quoted && String(quoted.status) === 'accepted'
      ? 'Your acceptance is recorded against the quotation.'
      : 'No acceptance is recorded.',
  },
  {
    key: 'payment',
    label: 'Payment',
    // NEVER REACHED, TODAY, FOR ANY APPLICATION — and that is a property of the
    // records rather than of this page. No invoice, order or payment in this
    // system carries a column pointing at an institutional application or its
    // agreement, so there is nothing this page could read that would make the
    // stage true. Rather than draw a stage that silently never turns, it is
    // drawn with the reason said in the applicant's own terms.
    reached: false,
    detail: 'MMAKF has not asked you for a payment through this page, and this page cannot show one. Any amount that becomes due will be invoiced to you directly by the federation office.',
  },
  {
    key: 'agreement',
    label: 'Agreement in place',
    reached: !!agreement,
    detail: agreement
      ? `Agreement ${agreement.ref}${agreement.signedAt ? `, signed ${when(agreement.signedAt)}` : ''}.`
      : 'No agreement has been signed.',
  },
  {
    key: 'delivery',
    label: 'In delivery',
    reached: String(programme?.status) === 'running',
    detail: String(programme?.status) === 'running'
      ? `Programme ${programme.code} is running.`
      : programme
        ? `Programme ${programme.code} is recorded and is not running.`
        : 'No programme has started.',
  },
  {
    key: 'complete',
    label: 'Complete',
    reached: String(programme?.status) === 'completed' || String(agreement?.status) === 'completed',
    detail: String(programme?.status) === 'completed' || String(agreement?.status) === 'completed'
      ? 'Delivery is recorded as finished.'
      : 'Not finished.',
  },
];

// When the case has ended, the route stops at the last thing that actually
// happened. Drawing the remaining rungs would be describing a journey this
// application is not going to take.
const lastReached = stages.reduce((m, st, i) => (st.reached ? i : m), -1);
const shownStages = hasEnded ? stages.slice(0, lastReached + 1) : stages;

const reductions = quoted
  ? Number(quoted.discountMinor ?? 0) + Number(quoted.concessionMinor ?? 0)
  : 0;
---

<Base
  title={`Application ${ref} — MMAKF`}
  description="The status of an MMAKF training application."
>
  {/* The noindex and no-referrer directives are set as RESPONSE HEADERS in the
      frontmatter above, not as <meta slot="head"> here. Base.astro defines no
      named head slot, so Astro discarded both of these silently and this page
      shipped with no robots directive at all. */}

  <div class="st">
    <div class="container st-inner">
      {failure ? (
        <>
          <p class="eyebrow">MMAKF training application</p>
          <h1 class="display-2">We cannot find that application.</h1>
          <p class="st-lede">{failure}</p>
          <p class="st-lede">
            If you have lost the link, write to
            {' '}<a href="mailto:admin@mmakf.in">admin@mmakf.in</a> with the name of
            your institution and MMAKF will resend it.
          </p>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={h('/learn')}>Back to training</a>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          {justSent && (
            <div class="st-sent" role="status">
              <strong>Your application has been sent.</strong>
              Keep this page — the address contains the key that opens it. It is
              the only way back in.
            </div>
          )}

          <p class="eyebrow">MMAKF training application</p>
          <h1 class="display-2">{view.institutionName}</h1>

          {isDraft && (
            <div class="st-draft" role="status">
              <strong>This application has not been sent yet.</strong>
              You reached step {resumeStep} of {TOTAL_STEPS}. Nothing has gone to
              MMAKF, and nothing will until you finish the form.
              <p class="st-draft-act">
                <a class="btn btn-primary" href={resumeHref}>Continue the application</a>
              </p>
            </div>
          )}

          <dl class="st-facts">
            <div>
              <dt>Reference</dt>
              <dd><code>{view.ref}</code></dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt>Stage</dt>
              {/* Drawn by Status and by nothing else, so `quoted` reads the
                  same word here as it does on the federation's own screens.
                  The dictionary's explanation is written for an administrator,
                  so it is not attached here — the timeline below carries the
                  sentence written for the applicant. */}
              <dd><Status value={view.status} domain="application" withMeaning={false} /></dd>
            </div>
            {view.submittedAt && (
              <div>
                <dt>Sent</dt>
                <dd>{when(view.submittedAt)}</dd>
              </div>
            )}
            {view.lastUpdateAt && (
              <div>
                <dt>Last update from MMAKF</dt>
                <dd>{when(view.lastUpdateAt)}</dd>
              </div>
            )}
            {/* The reference of a quotation that has actually been ISSUED.
                Deliberately not shown while one is only being prepared: a
                reference the school has received no document for is a number
                they would quote down the telephone and nobody would recognise. */}
            {quoted && quoteRef && (
              <div>
                <dt>Quotation</dt>
                <dd><code>{quoteRef}</code></dd>
              </div>
            )}
            {/* Rendered ONLY when the federation has actually undertaken a
                response time. It has published none, so this row is normally
                absent — rather than showing an invented date. */}
            {view.respondBy && (
              <div>
                <dt>MMAKF has undertaken to respond by</dt>
                <dd>{when(view.respondBy)}</dd>
              </div>
            )}
          </dl>

          {commercialProblem && (
            <p class="st-note st-note-boxed" role="status">{commercialProblem}</p>
          )}

          {/* ── THE ROUTE ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
          {!isDraft && shownStages.length > 0 && (
            <section class="st-chain-sec">
              <h2 class="st-h2">Where your request is</h2>
              <p class="st-lede">
                {hasEnded
                  ? 'This application has been closed. The steps below are the ones it actually reached; MMAKF has drawn no further ones, because there are none to come.'
                  : 'This is the route an MMAKF training request takes. A step is ticked when something has actually been recorded against it — it is not a schedule, and reaching one step is not a promise of the next.'}
              </p>

              <ol class="st-chain">
                {shownStages.map((st) => (
                  <li class:list={['st-step', st.reached ? 'is-done' : 'is-todo']}>
                    <span class="st-mark" aria-hidden="true">{st.reached ? '✓' : ''}</span>
                    <div class="st-step-body">
                      <p class="st-step-label">
                        {st.label}
                        <span class="st-step-state">{st.reached ? 'Done' : 'Not yet'}</span>
                      </p>
                      <p class="st-step-detail">{st.detail}</p>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ol>
            </section>
          )}

          {/* ── THE QUOTATION ───────────────────────────────────────────── */}
          {!isDraft && (
            <section class="st-quote-sec">
              <h2 class="st-h2">Your quotation</h2>

              {!quoted ? (
                <p class="st-lede">
                  {firstQuotationInProgress
                    ? 'MMAKF has started a quotation for this request and has not issued it to you yet. When it is issued it will appear here, itemised — every line, what it is for and how it was worked out.'
                    : 'No quotation has been issued for this application yet. When one is, it will appear here in full: every line, what it is for and how it was worked out. Until then there is no amount, and this page will not show you one.'}
                </p>
              ) : quoted.requiresManualQuote ? (
                <>
                  {/* NO FIGURE. Not a zero, not a range, not an estimate. */}
                  <div class="st-manual" role="note">
                    <strong>This quotation carries no amount.</strong>
                    <p>
                      No published MMAKF fee rule covered what you asked for, so
                      nothing was calculated and there is no figure to show you.
                      MMAKF will price this request by hand and send you the
                      amount separately.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                      This is not a fault and it is not an amount of nothing. It
                      means the federation has not published a fee that applies
                      to your request.
                    </p>
                  </div>
                  <dl class="st-facts">
                    <div>
                      <dt>Quotation</dt>
                      <dd><code>{quoteRef}</code> version {quoted.version}</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Status</dt>
                      <dd><Status value={quoted.status} domain="quote" withMeaning={false} /></dd>
                    </div>
                  </dl>
                </>
              ) : (
                <>
                  <dl class="st-facts">
                    <div>
                      <dt>Quotation</dt>
                      <dd><code>{quoteRef}</code> version {quoted.version}</dd>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Status</dt>
                      <dd><Status value={quoted.status} domain="quote" withMeaning={false} /></dd>
                    </div>
                    {quoted.issuedAt && (
                      <div>
                        <dt>Issued</dt>
                        <dd>{when(quoted.issuedAt)}</dd>
                      </div>
                    )}
                    {/* Only when one was actually set. MMAKF has published no
                        standard quotation validity, so most carry none — and a
                        quotation with no expiry date does not expire. */}
                    {quoted.validUntil && (
                      <div>
                        <dt>Valid until</dt>
                        <dd>{when(quoted.validUntil)}</dd>
                      </div>
                    )}
                  </dl>

                  {quoteLines.length === 0 ? (
                    <p class="st-lede">
                      This quotation has a total and no recorded working. MMAKF
                      can explain how it was reached — write to the address below
                      quoting the reference.
                    </p>
                  ) : (
                    <div class="st-table-wrap">
                      <table class="st-table">
                        <caption class="sr-only">
                          Quotation {quoteRef} version {quoted.version}, line by line
                        </caption>
                        <thead>
                          <tr>
                            <th scope="col">What it is for</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">Working</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">Amount</th>
                            <th scope="col" class="num">Running total</th>
                          </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                          {quoteLines.map((l: any) => (
                            <tr class:list={[l.amountMinor < 0 && 'is-credit']}>
                              <th scope="row">{l.label}</th>
                              <td class="num">{lineWorking(l) || '—'}</td>
                              <td class="num">{money(l.amountMinor, quoted.currency)}</td>
                              <td class="num">{money(l.runningTotalMinor, quoted.currency)}</td>
                            </tr>
                          ))}
                        </tbody>
                        <tfoot>
                          <tr>
                            <th scope="row" colspan="3">Subtotal</th>
                            <td class="num">{money(quoted.subtotalMinor, quoted.currency)}</td>
                          </tr>
                          {/* Stored NEGATIVE, so it prints with its own sign and
                              the arithmetic above still adds up on the page. */}
                          {reductions !== 0 && (
                            <tr>
                              <th scope="row" colspan="3">Reductions applied</th>
                              <td class="num">{money(reductions, quoted.currency)}</td>
                            </tr>
                          )}
                          {Number(quoted.taxMinor ?? 0) !== 0 && (
                            <tr>
                              <th scope="row" colspan="3">Tax</th>
                              <td class="num">{money(quoted.taxMinor, quoted.currency)}</td>
                            </tr>
                          )}
                          <tr class="is-total">
                            <th scope="row" colspan="3">Total</th>
                            <td class="num">{money(quoted.totalMinor, quoted.currency)}</td>
                          </tr>
                        </tfoot>
                      </table>
                    </div>
                  )}

                  <p class="st-note">
                    Every line above is the federation's own record of how this
                    figure was reached, in the order it was worked out. Nothing
                    on this page is rounded or restated: the amounts are the ones
                    stored against the quotation.
                  </p>
                </>
              )}

              {revisionInProgress && (
                <p class="st-note st-note-boxed" role="status">
                  MMAKF is preparing a revised version of this quotation. It has
                  not been issued, so no amount for it is shown here — the figures
                  above are the ones that stand until a revision reaches you.
                </p>
              )}
            </section>
          )}

          {/* ── DELIVERY ────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
          {!isDraft && (agreement || programme) && (
            <section class="st-quote-sec">
              <h2 class="st-h2">Agreement and delivery</h2>
              <dl class="st-facts">
                {agreement && (
                  <>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Agreement</dt>
                      <dd>
                        <code>{agreement.ref}</code>
                        {' '}<Status value={agreement.status} domain="contract" withMeaning={false} />
                      </dd>
                    </div>
                    {agreement.startsOn && (
                      <div>
                        <dt>Runs from</dt>
                        <dd>{when(agreement.startsOn)}{agreement.endsOn ? ` to ${when(agreement.endsOn)}` : ''}</dd>
                      </div>
                    )}
                  </>
                )}
                {programme && (
                  <>
                    <div>
                      <dt>Programme</dt>
                      <dd>
                        {programme.title} <code>{programme.code}</code>
                        {' '}<Status value={programme.status} domain="program" withMeaning={false} />
                      </dd>
                    </div>
                    {programme.startsOn && (
                      <div>
                        <dt>Delivery dates</dt>
                        <dd>{when(programme.startsOn)}{programme.endsOn ? ` to ${when(programme.endsOn)}` : ''}</dd>
                      </div>
                    )}
                    {programme.sessionsPlanned != null && (
                      <div>
                        <dt>Sessions planned</dt>
                        <dd>{programme.sessionsPlanned}</dd>
                      </div>
                    )}
                  </>
                )}
              </dl>
            </section>
          )}

          <section class="st-timeline">
            <h2 class="st-h2">Progress</h2>
            <CaseTimeline
              entries={view.timeline}
              domain="application"
              label={`Progress of application ${view.ref}`}
              empty={isDraft
                ? 'Nothing has been recorded yet. Your answers are saved, and this page will show each step once the application is sent.'
                : 'Nothing has been recorded against this application yet.'}
            />
            {!view.respondBy && !isDraft && (
              /* Said outright rather than left as an absence. A school that
                 sees no date assumes one exists and that this page is simply
                 not showing it, and then waits against a deadline nobody set.
                 MMAKF has published no response time, and that is the fact. */
              <p class="st-note">
                MMAKF has not published a response time for institutional
                applications, so this page shows no target date. Each step
                appears above once it has actually happened.
              </p>
            )}
          </section>

          <section class="st-help">
            <h2 class="st-h2">Something to add?</h2>
            <p class="st-lede">
              Write to <a href="mailto:admin@mmakf.in">admin@mmakf.in</a> quoting
              {' '}<code>{view.ref}</code>. It reaches the administrator handling
              your application.
            </p>
          </section>
        </>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .st { padding: 96px 0 80px; }
  .st-inner { max-width: 44rem; }
  .st-lede { color: var(--muted); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); max-width: 58ch; margin: 14px 0; }
  .st-h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: var(--text-lg); margin: 0 0 14px; }
  code {
    font-family: var(--font-accent, monospace);
    background: var(--bg-2); padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: var(--radius-xs); font-size: .95em;
  }

  .st-sent, .st-draft {
    padding: var(--space-5); margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); background: var(--card);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }
  .st-sent strong, .st-draft strong { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }
  .st-draft { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .st-draft-act { margin: var(--space-4) 0 0; }

  .st-facts { margin: var(--space-6) 0 0; display: grid; gap: 0; }
  .st-facts > div {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 18rem) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 4px var(--space-5); padding: 13px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .st-facts dt { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  .st-facts dd { margin: 0; }

  /* ── The route ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     A ladder of steps REACHED. A step that has not happened carries no date
     and no estimate — the federation has published no service standard, and a
     greyed-out step with a date beside it would be a promise nobody made. */
  .st-chain-sec { margin-top: var(--space-12); }
  .st-chain { list-style: none; margin: var(--space-6) 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .st-step {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.6rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 0 var(--space-4); padding: 14px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .st-step:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .st-mark {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    width: 1.35rem; height: 1.35rem; margin-top: 2px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 50%;
    font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1;
  }
  .st-step.is-done .st-mark { border-color: var(--gold); color: var(--gold); }
  .st-step-label {
    margin: 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
  }
  .st-step-state {
    font-size: var(--text-xs); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .st-step.is-todo .st-step-label { color: var(--muted); }
  .st-step-detail {
    margin: 4px 0 0; color: var(--muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); max-width: 58ch;
  }

  /* ── The quotation ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
  .st-quote-sec { margin-top: var(--space-12); }

  .st-manual {
    padding: var(--space-5); margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold); background: var(--card);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }
  .st-manual strong { display: block; margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .st-manual p { margin: 0 0 var(--space-3); color: var(--muted); line-height: var(--leading-relaxed); }
  .st-manual p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  /* A quotation is wide and a phone is not. It scrolls inside its own box
     rather than pushing the page sideways. */
  .st-table-wrap { margin: var(--space-6) 0 0; overflow-x: auto; }
  .st-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .st-table th, .st-table td { padding: 11px var(--space-3); text-align: left; }
  .st-table thead th {
    font-size: var(--text-xs); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em;
    color: var(--muted); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-weight: 400;
  }
  .st-table tbody th { font-weight: 400; }
  .st-table tbody tr { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .st-table .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .st-table tbody tr.is-credit td, .st-table tbody tr.is-credit th { color: var(--gold-2); }
  .st-table tfoot th, .st-table tfoot td { color: var(--muted); }
  .st-table tfoot tr.is-total th, .st-table tfoot tr.is-total td {
    color: var(--white); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 1.02rem;
  }

  .st-timeline { margin-top: var(--space-12); }

  .st-note {
    margin: var(--space-6) 0 0;
    padding-top: var(--space-4);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .st-note-boxed {
    border-top: 0; border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    background: var(--card); padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-5);
  }

  .st-help { margin-top: var(--space-12); padding-top: var(--space-6); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .st { padding: 78px 0 60px; }
    .st-facts > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2px; align-items: start; }
    .st-facts dt { font-size: .78rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .05em; }
  }
</style>
